["complications","An older adult with severe diarrhea becomes hypotensive and confused, with little urine output. Which complication best explains the deterioration?","High-volume diarrhea is followed by hypotension and oliguria. Which complication should be suspected?","Hypovolemia causing impaired organ perfusion","Large intestinal fluid losses can compromise circulation.","Esophageal varices caused by portal hypertension","This does not follow directly from the stated fluid losses.","Acute pancreatitis causing fat necrosis","The history identifies large fluid losses, not pancreatic inflammation.","Tophaceous gout caused by acute stool water loss alone","Tophi reflect chronic urate deposition, not this immediate deterioration."],
["tests","A patient has diarrhea, dizziness, and diminished urine output. Which initial tests help evaluate the consequences of fluid loss?","Which laboratory results are most relevant to high-volume diarrhea with oliguria?","Electrolytes, bicarbonate, blood urea nitrogen, and creatinine","These assess metabolic losses and renal consequences of reduced perfusion.","An isolated serum uric acid measurement","This cannot characterize the primary fluid-loss complications.","A lower esophageal sphincter pressure study","This evaluates esophageal motility.","A screening bone-density measurement","This does not assess acute dehydration."],
["management","A patient with frequent watery stools is lightheaded and has a dry tongue. Which nursing priority addresses the immediate deficit?","Diarrhea is causing symptomatic fluid loss. What should the treatment plan prioritize?","Replace fluids and electrolytes as prescribed and investigate the cause","Rehydration addresses the deficit while cause-directed care prevents ongoing loss.","Delay fluid replacement until every stool study returns","Dehydration requires timely correction.","Encourage continued use of a suspected causative laxative","This may prolong the losses.","Restrict all oral and intravenous fluids indefinitely","This can worsen hypovolemia."]
