["management","A patient has recurrent symptomatic gallstones and asks about definitive treatment. Which procedure may be recommended after assessment?","Which procedure commonly treats recurrent symptomatic gallbladder stones?","Cholecystectomy","Removing the gallbladder can address recurrent symptomatic disease.","Esophageal myotomy","This treats an esophageal outflow disorder.","Colectomy in every uncomplicated case","The diseased structure is not the colon.","Joint arthroplasty","This does not treat biliary disease."]
