["management","An admitted pancreatitis patient is tachycardic and vomiting. Which early nursing priority is appropriate?","Which assessment guides safe initial supportive care in acute pancreatitis?","Monitor perfusion, fluid status, pain, and organ dysfunction","Supportive management requires repeated reassessment of severity and response.","Encourage continued alcohol consumption","Alcohol can worsen pancreatic injury.","Ignore urine output during fluid treatment","Urine output helps assess perfusion and response.","Give unrestricted high-fat meals despite active vomiting","Nutrition must match clinical tolerance and the treatment plan."]
